<p>The town of San Lorenzo de El Escorial, which grew up around the monastery, has its own quiet appeal beyond the complex itself, with cafés and restaurants serving straightforward Castilian food in the streets surrounding the main square. Its elevated position in the foothills of the Sierra de Guadarrama also means noticeably cooler air than central Madrid, particularly appreciated by visitors making the trip in the height of summer.</p>
